@page "/guide"
<PageTitle>Invoice Explorer | Operator guide</PageTitle>
<section class="page-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">OPERATING PRINCIPLES</p><h1>Better extraction. Honest measurement.</h1><p class="subtitle">Understand what the pipeline does before acting on its output.</p></div></section>
<article class="panel report-panel operator-guide">
    <h2>1. Start with the original</h2><p>The first pass uses your original PDF and the configured invoice model. Digital text, layout, and all returned fields are retained. Optional fallback passes query unresolved fields, enable high-resolution OCR, re-render scanned pages, or use a trained custom model. They stop at the configured pass limit.</p>
    <h2>2. Escalate selectively</h2><p>Query fields and high-resolution OCR are paid add-ons. They require the actual S0 resource tier and an explicit configuration switch. Query fields extend the schema; repeating native field names is not a guarantee of better accuracy. Rasterization remains off by default because it may degrade text-rich PDFs.</p>
    <h2>3. Read the decision correctly</h2><p><b>Ready</b> means every required field is present, every extracted target field meets the policy, and no blocking validation issue is present. <b>Review</b> means extraction completed but needs a person to resolve uncertainty. <b>Failed</b> is a processing error. <b>Ambiguous</b> means a submission might have reached Azure; automatic resubmission is deliberately blocked.</p>
    <p>Different values across passes produce a conflict. Agreement is supporting evidence, not independent statistical proof. Azure scores are never averaged together to invent a stronger score for one field. Optional missing fields remain visible in coverage.</p>
    <h2 id="evaluation">4. Establish a representative benchmark</h2><p>Review original invoices from different vendors, layouts, languages, scan qualities, and page counts. Use <b>Calibration</b> labels to choose rules and thresholds. Keep a separate <b>Test</b> set untouched during tuning. Avoid putting nearly identical invoices from the same template in both splits.</p>
    <p>Value accuracy compares exact normalized values on fields labeled as present. Missing predictions count as errors. Verified absence is reported separately so empty fields cannot inflate the main accuracy number. The baseline is the original PDF pass on the same labeled fields. Failed latest executions stay in the evaluation denominator.</p>
    <p>The 95% Wilson lower bound is descriptive; field observations within the same invoice are correlated. A small or unrepresentative benchmark does not prove a 98% production accuracy rate. Review critical fields and examine results by vendor and document type before adopting thresholds.</p>
    <h2>5. Operate a large batch</h2><p>Configure <code>appsettings.local.json</code> in the workspace. Run <code>doctor</code>, then <code>plan --all</code>. Check the page volume and request budget before <code>extract --all</code>. The console prints a batch ID. Use <code>resume BATCH_ID</code> after interruption. Use <code>--rerun</code> intentionally for a new extraction history under the same configuration.</p>
    <p>F0 mode processes one document and its first two pages. S0 is required for full batches. Requests are paced across workers; each source is identified by SHA-256. Duplicate files and completed results under the same configuration are skipped. Raw responses, normalized fields, business CSV, and review history are retained locally.</p>
    <h2>6. Improve the model, not just the score</h2><p>When OCR is poor, obtain a clearer scan or evaluate the raster/high-resolution alternatives. When OCR is good but field assignment is wrong, label representative vendor layouts and train a Document Intelligence custom model in your approved Azure environment. Configure its model ID and give the custom pass enough room in MaxPasses. Training and its data remain in the client environment.</p>
    <p>Never correct a total merely to make an arithmetic check pass, guess a tax identifier, or infer a currency from a dollar symbol alone. Record the observed evidence and let review resolve ambiguity.</p>
</article>
